ProsperoSunshine PS4: refuse a second device at /resume (single capture channel)

The PS4 host has one PBS capture channel and one virtual controller, so only one device can stream at a time. launch()
already refuses a second client while the app runs ("An app is already running on this host"), but resume() inherited the
PS5 join path from 0013-join-with-matching-hdr: a different paired device that picks "Resume" on the busy host was let
through, because video::hdr_conflict() is a stub on PS4 (one channel, no HDR conflict to report). Two sessions against the
single warm PBS capture then race for frames and thrash the one virtual pad. Refuse the join here instead, with a message
Moonlight shows. Same-cert resume (an ordinary reconnect) has session_count_except_cert() == 0 and is unaffected. With
this, two different-cert sessions can never coexist, so the quit-with-another-player branch (0012) is unreachable on PS4.

--- a/src/nvhttp.cpp
+++ b/src/nvhttp.cpp
@@ -1792,20 +1792,15 @@
     }
 
 #ifdef __SCE__
-    // A device that joins another device's stream gets its picture, unless a capture channel of its own is free. One that
-    // asks for another dynamic range than every running stream while none is free is turned away here, where Moonlight
-    // shows the reason, and not after its stream has started.
+    // ProsperoSunshine PS4: one capture channel and one virtual pad, so only one device streams at a time. A different
+    // device that picks "Resume" on the busy host is refused here, with a message Moonlight shows, instead of joining and
+    // racing the running device for capture frames and the controller. Same-cert resume (a reconnect) is not caught here.
     if (rtsp_stream::session_count_except_cert(client->cert) > 0) {
-      const bool wants_hdr = util::from_view(get_arg(args, "hdrMode", "0")) != 0;
-      if (const auto running_hdr = video::hdr_conflict(wants_hdr)) {
-        BOOST_LOG(warning) << "Resume refused: both capture channels run "sv << (*running_hdr ? "in HDR"sv : "without HDR"sv);
-        tree.put("root.resume", 0);
-        tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_code", 409);
-        tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_message", *running_hdr ?
-          "Another device is streaming in HDR. Turn HDR on in Moonlight to join." :
-          "Another device is streaming without HDR. Turn HDR off in Moonlight to join.");
-        return;
-      }
+      BOOST_LOG(warning) << "Resume refused: another device is already streaming (single capture channel)"sv;
+      tree.put("root.resume", 0);
+      tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_code", 409);
+      tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_message", "Another device is already streaming this host. Only one device can connect at a time.");
+      return;
     }
 #endif
 
